<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Caishi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1161</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jin-song-wars">Jin–Song wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Caishi was fought in November 1161 on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze River</a> near Caishi, in present-day Anhui, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Southern Song</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchens">Jurchen</a> Jin. The Jin emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wanyan-liang">Wanyan Liang</a>, Prince Hailing, tried to cross the river with a large army, but Song warships, including paddle-wheel boats, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gunpowder">gunpowder</a> bombs defeated his fleet. The failure led to his murder by his own officers and secured the Song frontier on the Huai.</p></div>
